T*
(Dimensioning is the art of providing precise numerical values of geometric sizes and) Tj
T*
(locations:) Tj
T*
(* Elements of Dimensioning: Extension line \(projects 2-3 mm past dimension line\),) Tj
T*
(Dimension line \(parallel to measured feature\), Arrowheads \(proportions 3:1 length to) Tj
T*
(width, fully filled\), Leader line \(thin line inclined at 30-60 deg ending in) Tj
T*
(horizontal landing of 2-3 mm\).) Tj
T*
(* Dimensioning Systems:) Tj
T*
(- 1. Aligned System: Dimensions placed parallel to and above dimension lines. Read from) Tj
T*
(bottom or right edge of sheet.) Tj
T*
(- 2. Unidirectional System: All dimensions placed horizontally, breaking the dimension) Tj
T*
(line near center. Read exclusively from the bottom.) Tj
T*
(* Golden Rules: Never cross dimension lines with other lines; dimension outer) Tj
T*
(features outside the view; avoid redundant dimensioning; dimension hidden features) Tj
T*
(only when unavoidable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
