(- LOS = RF x ML = \(1 / 50\) x 6 m = \(1 / 50\) x 600 cm = 12.0 cm.) Tj
T*
(* Step 2: Main Scale Division:) Tj
T*
(- Draw a horizontal rectangle of length 12 cm and width 1 cm.) Tj
T*
(- Divide the 12 cm length into 6 equal parts using acute angle line division method.) Tj
T*
(Each part represents 1 meter \(12 cm / 6 = 2 cm per meter\).) Tj
T*
(- Number the main divisions: Label the first division mark from left as 0, then 1, 2, 3,) Tj
T*
(4, 5 to the right.) Tj
T*
(* Step 3: Sub-Division of First Main Division:) Tj
T*
(- The leftmost 1-meter division \(from 0 to the left\) is divided into 10 equal parts.) Tj
T*
(Each sub-part represents 1 decimeter \(0.1 m\).) Tj
T*
(- Label sub-divisions to the left: 0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 decimeters.) Tj
T*
(* Step 4: Marking the Target Distance \(4.7 meters\):) Tj
T*
(- From the 0 mark, extend a measurement 4 units to the right \(4 meters\).) Tj
T*
(- From the 0 mark, extend 7 units to the left \(7 decimeters = 0.7 meters\).) Tj
T*
(- Total measured distance = 4 m + 0.7 m = 4.7 m. Draw extension lines and dimension line) Tj
T*
(with arrows and label 4.7 m.) Tj
T*
